  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nAreawide rain showers and gusty winds 25-30 MPH continue through\nthis afternoon and evening as a surface trough remains draped\nacross the region. As the trough continues to sink south across\nNorthern Ohio, rain showers will transition into lake effect\nrain downwind of Lake Erie and Lake Huron tonight into early\nSaturday morning. Given the Lake Huron connection, the primary\narea of lake effect rain showers will remain situated between\nthe I-71 and I-77 corridors. Any remaining gusty winds will\ngradually diminish through the overnight hours as high pressure\ngradually builds into the region. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \nAforementioned high pressure will build into the area from the\nwest this weekend leading to a period of dry but cold\nconditions. Effective radiative cooling under the high on\nSaturday night will lead to widespread low temperatures in the\nlow to mid 30s and possibly the upper 20s in some locations. A\nFreeze Watch has been issued for nearly all zones in the\nforecast area with the exception of Lake County and the\nlakeshore zones of Ashtabula and Erie County PA where lows may\nbe a bit warmer given the proximity to the relatively warmer\nwaters of Lake Erie. Temperatures will begin to moderate into\nearly next week as high pressure builds to the east of the\nregion.",
